<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA5-QA2-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA5-QA2-001" ;
  triage:title "code_mask() in .just/rust_source.py treats every lifetime tick as a char-literal opener, masking list_messages from the read-concurrency-gates CI check" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-2, PR #1407 @ 7997f8aaa. read-concurrency-gates CI check fails: 'AV.3 read-concurrency gate could not inspect source: read handler list_messages is missing.' Root cause in .just/rust_source.py's code_mask(): it lexes Rust with a naive single-quote scanner with no concept of lifetime syntax, treating the ' in '+ Send + '_>>' as opening a char literal and masking everything until the next literal quote. Pre-existing bug, newly exposed because BA.5 added a new pub(crate) fn dispatch(...) inherent method (reusing the same lifetime pattern) positioned before list_messages in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs, so the masking span now swallows list_messages's definition. list_messages itself is present, correct, unchanged, and correctly read-only -- this is a lint-tool defect, not a BA.5 code defect, but it currently blocks CI green. fenix's ruling (PR #1407, issuecomment-5643452062): STANDS, fix on this branch (BA5-FIX-R2-1789187300, cipher). Fix the lexer: a ' followed by an identifier-start char and not closed by a matching ' two characters later (and not a backslash escape) is a lifetime/label and must not be masked. Add a .just/tests case for '_>> / 'a / 'x' / '\n'. Do not just reorder dispatch below list_messages -- that leaves the bug for the next file. fenix classifies this important (not minor) because it currently blocks merge." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci-gate" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T04:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "feature/ba5-queue-ephemeral-item frozen by fenix's ruling (2026-09-12T04:37:03Z, per Rand: a branch is not touched again once its minimum functionality for closure is complete); BA5-FIX-R2 cancelled, cipher told not to push. Further promoted by fenix's cleanup ruling (ATM 2026-09-12T04:44:29Z): worktree layer 5, fix/phase-ba-cleanup (new gh-stack layer above docs/ba6, cipher single writer) -- arch-ctm's BA6-CLEANUP task is cancelled; fix lands once on the cleanup layer, not on docs/ba6." ;
  triage:promoteTo "fix/phase-ba-cleanup" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA5 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T04:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
